test_datapath_params_match_the_instance:
  [gate 23m] 5 real milan_soc.py elaborations in 5 s: for every config the integer parameters Instance("milan_datapath") receives are exactly eb.datapath_params(), the shapes the publication census elaborates; every other keyword is a ROM image path
test_datapath_params_gate_bites:
  [gate 23m mutation] 3/3 cuts rejected in 4 s, each naming its keyword: a binding dropped to 0, a value one short, and a keyword the builder does not state
test_every_recipe_elaborates:
  [gate 23g] 5/5 shipped recipes reach Instance("milan_datapath") in 4 s, each with the flow tail its own launcher appends (--build included, the flag every shape gate excludes). This proves a recipe RUNS, not that it builds the SoC its config describes - that comparison is gate 1e's and #155 carries where the two disagree
test_recipe_smoke_gate_bites:
  [gate 23g mutation] 2/2 recipes stripped of --entity-gen-dir refused to elaborate, which is #156 item 1 replayed on the recipes that shipped it
test_optional_blocks_reach_the_instance:
  [gate 23f] 8 real milan_soc.py elaborations of endstation_ax7101_1x1_tdm8, the shipping AX shape, in 6 s: each of the 7 --no-* flags lands as p_<PARAM>=0 in the Instance("milan_datapath") parameters and moves NOTHING else, a build that prunes nothing passes none of them (16 parameters, byte-identical top .v). Fabric gPTP's product default is graded separately by gate 1e. This grades what elaboration HANDS the module, not what the module DOES with it (gate 23d) and not that the bitstream places or boots
test_optional_block_instance_gate_bites:
  [gate 23f mutation] 8/8 broken links of the argv -> Instance chain rejected in 13 s: a dropped CLI handoff, two dropped constructor keywords, a dropped keyword inside add_milan_datapath, a suppressed parameter, a renamed parameter, and both prune polarities inverted; gate 1e separately owns the profile-aware gPTP chain
test_optional_block_consumption_gate_bites:
  [gate 23d mutation] 7/7 disconnected --no-* handoffs rejected by block name
  [gate 23d mutation] 6/6 dedicated keywords MilanSoC.__init__ never declares rejected by block name (LiteX warns and ignores; the bitstream ships unpruned)
  [gate 23d chain] 10/10 cut links between main() and `dp_params[f"p_{param}"] = 0` rejected, the three that would prune an UNFLAGGED build included
test_gptp_plane_reaches_the_instance:
  [gate 1e] 8 real elaborations: the product fabric default is identical across product shapes and to explicit ON; bare-metal option-OFF elaborates as announced verification-only hardware (#259); build.sh, sweep.sh and deploy.sh ship fabric ownership
test_gptp_plane_instance_gate_bites:
  [gate 1e mutation] 6/6 owner-carrier cuts rejected
test_clock_plan_reaches_the_instance:
  [gate 23l] 4 real milan_soc.py elaborations of endstation_ax7101_1x1_tdm8 in 4 s: --audio-fs-hz and --audio-word-bits land as p_AUDIO_IF_FS_HZ_P / p_AUDIO_IF_WORD_BITS_P and move p_AUDIO_IF_CLK_HZ_P (2 x SLOTS x slot bits x fs) with them, singly and together, moving NOTHING else; at the declared shipping values both are ABSENT, so the tracked configs' top .v is byte-identical to the build before #399. This grades what elaboration HANDS the module, not that the bitstream places or boots
test_clock_plan_instance_gate_bites:
  [gate 23l mutation] 7/7 broken links of the declaration -> Instance chain rejected in 11 s: a dropped CLI handoff, a dropped constructor keyword, a dropped keyword inside add_milan_datapath, a suppressed parameter, a renamed parameter, a bit clock that stopped following the declaration, and a parameter passed at the default
